From b3001c201411b4e2b8ccfc23c39afd833da2cac3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 00:02:18 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] [third_party/pkg] Add Architecture.ppc64 and the
 linux_ppc64 target

Class: upstreamable fix (to dart-lang/native). This is the lib/ part of
patches/dart-lang-native/0001-code_assets-hooks_runner-Add-Architecture.ppc64.patch,
applied with -p3 to the vendored code_assets 1.0.0 and hooks_runner 1.0.1.
The tests, the JSON schema and the generated syntax it also changes live
in that patch; they ran in a dart-lang/native checkout at
hooks_runner-v1.0.1 (code_assets: 479 tests, hooks_runner test/model: 10).

* code_assets: Architecture.ppc64 ('ppc64'), in Architecture.values and
  ArchitectureSyntax. Architecture.fromAbi and Architecture.current fall
  back to architectureFromAbiName(abi.toString()) for an ABI the constant
  table cannot name.
* hooks_runner: Target.linuxPpc64 is looked up by name in Abi.values and
  is null on SDKs without that ABI; Target.values includes it when
  present; Target.os falls back to Target.osFromAbiName.

Abi.linuxPpc64 exists only in the ppc64 port of the Dart SDK. Nothing
here names it as a constant, so both packages still compile on, and are
unchanged on, the stock SDK that runs the flutter_tools tests. The
contract with the SDK port is that Abi.linuxPpc64.toString() is
'linux_ppc64' (_Architecture.ppc64, as dart:ffi names architectures).
